Is it possible to add a fallback to legacy method "getSystemCpuLoad", in my test it worked fine.

```
import java.lang.management.ManagementFactory;

public class CpuTest {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("=== JVM CPU Metric Debugger (Java 25 / Temurin) ===");

        // Grab standard platform bean
        java.lang.management.OperatingSystemMXBean standardBean = ManagementFactory.getOperatingSystemMXBean();

        // Cast to the Extended management MXBean explicitly for full access
        if (standardBean instanceof com.sun.management.OperatingSystemMXBean extendedBean) {
            System.out.printf("%-30s: %.4f\n", "System CPU Load (Legacy)", extendedBean.getSystemCpuLoad());
            System.out.printf("%-30s: %.4f\n", "Cpu Load (Modern)", extendedBean.getCpuLoad());
            System.out.printf("%-30s: %.4f\n", "Process CPU Load", extendedBean.getProcessCpuLoad());
            System.out.printf("%-30s: %d\n", "Available Processors", extendedBean.getAvailableProcessors());
        } else {
            System.out.println("Error: MXBean is not an instance of com.sun.management.OperatingSystemMXBean");
        }
    }
}
```

